         <title><![CDATA[Lockdowns are happening at Whitehorse jail for wrong reasons, advocates say]]></title>
         <link>https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/north/lockdowns-are-happening-at-whitehorse-jail-for-wrong-reasons-advocates-say-9.7416639?cmp=rss</link>
         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/9f8de511-f3be-486d-a9c1-e8c67800e6e8,1794350684309/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C378%2C4032%2C2268%29%3B' alt='The Whitehorse Correctional Centre' width='620' height='349' title='During lockdowns, inmates are confined to their cells. In one unit, Legal Services found inmates were locked down an extra 80 hours a month, on average.'/><p>Inmates at Whitehorse Correctional Centre faced unscheduled lockdowns almost every second day this year, adding up to hundreds of additional hours confined to their cells. Lawyers say that affects mental health, access to programming and court proceedings.</p>]]></description>
